        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "“R13, R14 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | When shorted, bridge J3-pin3 and J8-pin3 together and onto the MAX3485 TTL bus” (page 1)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Following the schematic's serial-mode instruction would alter the MAX3485 control network rather than configure the servo signal path, potentially preventing serial-servo communication. The actual jumper references appear to be R21 and R23, so the assembly instruction is inconsistent with the drawn circuit.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The serial-servo jumper instruction conflicts with the component values and locations shown: R13/R14 are control-network resistors, while R21/R23 appear to be the 0-ohm signal-path links. An assembler following the instruction could misconfigure the transceiver and leave serial servos inoperative."
}

